From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:12:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/30] drama: incremental codec decode, bit-identical to the
 whole decode

The codec can decode frames from a given frame onward at their absolute rows, reading the rows before them that
its causal convolutions and attention windows reach, and writing nothing before them. Every chunk boundary gives
the same samples as one decode of all frames, so audio can be decoded while it is generated.
